#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Interaction Metrics Analyzer  (v2)
=======================================

Analyzes interactions.csv (one or many daily dumps) and produces the metrics
requested in the 27-Aug meeting notes.

Metric map (matches the manager's numbered asks)
------------------------------------------------
M1  Total number of problems encountered            -> problem clusters
M2  Total number of intents / sub-intents generated -> intent clusters (NLP)
M3  Total workflows stated + tools called per workflow
M4  Is the cluster similar, or is a NEW workflow generated every time for the
    same intent?   -> workflow reuse / divergence, the "6 intents vs 100
    workflows" test
M5  A API calls: agent side vs tool side, parallel fan-out, co-occurrence
M6  Baseline: volume in the July window, +ve vs -ve samples

Design principles
-----------------
- Standard library ONLY (no pandas / sklearn needed)
- No hardcoded interaction count, intent name, tool name, MSISDN or column order
- Nested JSON inside CSV cells is decoded recursively
- Streaming CSV read; large JSON cells supported (field size limit raised)
- Every threshold / pattern is a CLI flag or a constant at the top

Usage
-----
    python A_metrics_analyzer.py interactions.csv
    python A_metrics_analyzer.py ./output_updated/output --output-dir ./metrics
    python A_metrics_analyzer.py interactions.csv \
        --start-date 2025-07-13 --end-date 2025-07-26 --only-positive
"""

